silm:instances_papers_09_minimal_category_theory_chapters_01_objects_and_arrows_sections_04_concrete_anchor_survey_concrete_anchor_13_DecimalValue42#decimalvalue4_2 silm:hasLongDescription "The DecimalValue4_2 is the decimal value 4.2 attached to the measurement event. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'DecimalValue4_2', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
